  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: 4beb055f07aaff244873dec698d0363e, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 14
    m_FontStyle: 3
    m_BestFit: 1
    m_MinSize: 10
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 1
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "City rates are key indicators that define the overall condition, events,
    and income of your metropolis. Keeping these rates within healthy ranges not
    only boosts your economy but also helps prevent negative events such as robberies
    or health crises.\n\nCrime Rate\n\nIt measures Level of unlawful activities driven
    by poverty, low education, and insufficient policing. High crime can trigger
    robberies; each successful robbery costs you money and shakes citizen trust.\n\nHow
    calculated:\n\nBase Crime: 20\n\nIncreases by 0.5 \xD7 Unemployment Rate\n\nDecreases
    by 0.2 \xD7 Education Rate and by (Number of Police Stations \xD7 10)\n\nSmoothed
    over time using a blending factor (\u03B1 = 0.1)\n\nResult clamped between 0\u2013100."
